age specific health and infrastructure initiatives. Most aid is now provided as grants rather than loans to avoid exacerbating recipient debt burdens, though loan guarantees remain a tool for specific strategic partners.\n\nGeographically, aid distribution reflects shifting U.S. strategic priorities. While the Middle East and North Africa historically received the largest share, the post-9/11 era saw a surge in funding for South and Central Asia (Afghanistan and Pakistan). By FY2017, Sub-Saharan Africa accounted for 25% of total aid, driven largely by health initiatives and humanitarian crises. Conversely, aid to Europe and Eurasia has declined significantly as former Soviet states graduated from assistance programs.\n\nDespite leading the world in total dollar volume of Official Development Assistance (ODA), the U.S. ranks low among major donors when measured as a percentage of Gross National Income (0.18% in 2017), falling short of the UN target of 0.7%. The report also highlights the "tied aid" controversy; approximately 32% of U.S. bilateral development assistance is tied to the purchase of U.S. goods and services, a practice that increases costs but is maintained to secure domestic political support.\n\nFinally, the report details the legislative framework, noting that while permanent authorization laws exist, Congress has not passed a comprehensive foreign aid authorization bill since 1985. Instead, policy and funding levels are primarily determined through annual appropriations, specifically the State, Foreign Operations, and Related Programs (SFOPS) bill. The use of the Overseas Contingency Operations (OCO) designation has allowed for increased funding for war-related aid without violating discretionary spending caps, though its future application remains uncertain. As the program continues to evolve, the U.S. faces challenges in balancing strategic interests, humanitarian needs, and the efficiency of aid delivery in a changing global landscape.', refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=None, audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[], reasoning=None), stop_reason=None, token_ids=None)], created=1786380970, model='Qwen3.5-27B', object='chat.completion', service_tier=None, system_fingerprint=None, usage=CompletionUsage(completion_tokens=753, prompt_tokens=13237, total_tokens=13990, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), prompt_logprobs=None, prompt_token_ids=None, kv_transfer_params=None)

